\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{One field at several depths}
\date{2026-11-28}

\p{A tower supplies a Gaussian probability at each depth and a
specified averaging map between consecutive depths. For the fixed-ratio
family, \ref{fdip-00C3} puts these fields on one probability space
so that each coarse field is the prescribed average of the finer one.
Does that construction require the geometric profile, or only the
compatibility just proved?}
